`,e.jsx(r.p,{children:"The previews retain every part of the source frame, including original game interfaces and input/output comparison labels. Only excerpt selection, proportional resizing, frame-rate normalization (maximum 30 fps), H.264 encoding, audio removal, and first-frame WebP poster encoding were applied to the six primary excerpts. Square footage and wide comparisons use a quiet matte instead of cutting off content. Native frame proportions are used in the lower gallery when practical. The mobile comparison variant additionally rearranges the two complete source panels as described below; it does not crop, replace, or generate any scene content."}),`
